CHANGES v1.9:
-------------
1: Handle changing is now implemented and pointers need not be run.  This was
   the original problem but all Handle pointers are now adjusted after a handle
   change.
2: All text is now external;  copy Uni-Edtext to SYSTEXT: and edit it to your
   liking.

CHANGES v2.0:
-------------
1: BUG FIX!!  Pointers were not being sorted correctly.. This is DEFINITELY
   fixed and no harm will be done by this version..   I tested it for 72 hours
   myself and also via my beta-testers.

CHANGES v2.2:
-------------
1. Minor Uni-Edtext change - Inf. Byte and Inf.File flag text was reversed.
2. Now changes online user's status IMMEDIATELY when edited.

CHANGES v3.0:
-------------
1. Now allows users to be killed.
2. Prevents ONLINE users from being killed.
3. Prevents the SYSOP's account from being killed.
4. More additions to SYSTEXT:Uni-Edtext

CHANGES 3.1:
------------
1. Reserve Account function has been added to allow the sysop to pre-logon
   a new user.
2. Uses the lowest, previously unused account for new user reservations.
3. Bug fixed where minutes per day prevously allowed up to 99, now allows up to
   255.

CHANGES 3.5:
------------
1. Bug fixed where last user was still specified as ONLINE.
2. Bug fixed where ByteCredits were displayed as LONG and not UNSIGNED causing
   negative ByteCredits.
3. Changes in Uni-Edtext, please make sure you make the changes before reporting
   any possible bugs.

CHANGES 3.6:
------------
1. Bug fix where assigning a new access group did not adopt the priveledges
   for the new access to the user.
2. Changes made to reflect the new MCI scheme.

CHANGES 3.7:
------------
1. CallBack @ Login flag support added.
2. Small formatting changes in the PRIVS sections of Uni-Edtext.
3. Now allows U[account number/handle] to load/edit a user at the main Uni-Ed prompt.
              ^^
               no spaces (maybe later :)

CHANGES 3.8:
------------
1. Recompiled for C-Net AMIGA v2.0
2. Now allows entering an account # at the main Uni-Ed prompt
   while still retaining the "U" funtion of the regular "load user"
   prompt.

CHANGES v5.10:
--------------
1: Recompiled for CNet v2.20!
2: Most of the new flags and options supported now.
3: Macro and signature editing capabilities implemented.
4: "Reserve User" function has been removed temporarily - will be
   re-implemented later, due to continuing interest in this function.

Options & flags not supported until I get the newest headers from Perspective:

	RECEIVE MAIL
	ALLOW WHO BANNER
	TERMLINK ACCESS
	PORT MONITOR ACCESS
	BIRTHDATE
	Changing of VOICE phone #.
	Access control of editing Handle, Name etc, Address, voice & data #'s.

CHANGES v5.20:
--------------
1: Many significant changes to the new configurable User List.
   (see the section titled USER LIST for more details)

Changes v6.0:
-------------
1: New CNet flags added:   Private Personal data (edit handle etc,..)
                           TermLink access
                           PortMonitor acess
                           TimeLock Exempt
                           ReceiveMail
                           Allow WHO Banner
2: Signatures that exist are now denoted with an asterisk (*)
3: If a blank signature is saved, you are given the option to delete
   the signature.
4: New format Hide/Muffle now supported.
5: New format Response pausing now supported.
6: A version string has now been added to allow you to find out the version
   number of uni-ed, using "Version uni-ed" from any CLI/Shell.

Changes v6.2:
-------------
1: if user has the "unlimited Credits" or "unlimited files" flags set,
   "NO LIMIT" is now displayed in BYTE CREDITS and/or FILE CREDITS.
   (The "NO LIMIT" text is editable in uni-edtext)
2: Minor cosmetic changes/fixes.


FUTURE PLANS:
-------------
All future improvements (not including header changes to CNet by Perspective
Software) will be concentrated on better priviledge flag organization,
addition of routines to edit ALL user dates, cutting code size without
sacrificing program efficiency, and other minor visual improvements.

Also, Uni-Ed's userllist will receive considerably more attention as to
what is displayed.
